he lesson idea about present?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Start from a specific textual clue, then explain its effect.","options":["Locate a specific word, phrase or structural clue before deciding.","Guess from the title alone with no textual clue.","Copy a model sentence from another story unchanged.","Treat a missing detail as a stated fact."],"question":"In a new text, what should you do first to practise story?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Repair means fixing meaning or evidence, not padding.","options":["Add adjectives without fixing the wrong idea.","Make the answer longer while keeping the same mistake.","Delete the evidence that disagreed with your first guess.","Change the inaccurate idea or missing evidence, not only the length."],"question":"Which revision actually repairs meaning?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Transfer needs fresh material with an explained language choice.","options":["Racing every sentence at one volume makes important beats hard to hear.","Use a fresh sentence or text and explain one precise choice about present.","Retype the worked model as the final answer.","Change fonts and claim the work is new."],"question":"Which response shows transfer of present to new material?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Require independently produced work with a specific supporting detail.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating present on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.","sample_answer":"Original response on new material: Pause after gone (problem beat); stress ticket or book depending on the reveal plan. Reasoning: I used present by attending to story rather than copying the worked model.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes t